<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ National-NZF govt table of fiscal parameters.</title>
<headline>NZ National-NZF govt table of fiscal parameters.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a table of the fiscal parameters worked out by the new National-New Zealand First coalition government:</p>
<p>					1996/97  1997/98  1998/99  1999/00</p>
<p>							$ millions</p>
<p>Revenue (incl SOE surplus)</p>
<p>DEFU projections		   35,719   35,904   37,404   39,176</p>
<p>Delay tax cut one yr			   1,100</p>
<p>Further tax cut from 1-Jul-99				     -1,000</p>
<p>					-------  -------  -------  -------</p>
<p>Total revenue			35,719   37,004   37,404   38,176</p>
<p>Pct of GDP			     37.3     36.7     35.5     34.3</p>
<p>Expense</p>
<p>DEFU projections		   33,226   32,779   32,999   33,069</p>
<p>Additional finance costs				    100	300</p>
<p>Additional coalition expense (1)	   1,200    1,700    2,100</p>
<p>					-------  -------  -------  -------</p>
<p>Total expense			 33,226  33,979   34,799   35,469</p>
<p>Pct of GDP				34.7    33.7     33.0     31.9</p>
<p>Operating balance</p>
<p>DEFU projections		     2,493   3,125    4,405    6,107</p>
<p>Pct of GDP				 2.6     3.1	4.2	5.5</p>
<p>Coalition				2,493   3,025    2,605    2,707</p>
<p>Pct of GDP				 2.6     3.0	2.5	2.4</p>
<p>Net debt</p>
<p>DEFU projections		    26,086  23,758   20,474   15,470</p>
<p>Pct of GDP				27.3    23.6     19.4     13.9</p>
<p>Coalition			     26,086  23,858   22,474   18,870</p>
<p>Pct of GDP				27.3    23.7     21.1     17.0</p>
<p>(1) Inclusive of cost to revenue of abolishing the surcharge</p>
<p>The table assumes that the DEFU economic projections remain appropriate.</p>
<p>The number provided for a further tax cut from July 1999 is broadly equivalent to 2 percent of the contribution base, for the compulsory savings scheme, in that year.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
